## Future Topic Ideas

### Digital Audio Fundamentals
- **Sampling & Nyquist theorem**: Why 44.1kHz? What happens when you undersample (aliasing demos)
- **Bit depth & quantization**: 16-bit vs 24-bit, quantization noise, dithering
- **Audio codecs**: How MP3/AAC exploit psychoacoustics to compress audio (perceptual coding, masking)

### Spatial Audio
- **Stereo and localization**: How two ears determine direction (ILD, ITD)
- **Binaural audio & HRTF**: 3D sound with headphones
- **Room acoustics**: Reverb, early reflections, RT60, absorption coefficients

### Sound Design & Synthesis
- **Synthesis techniques**: Additive, subtractive, FM, wavetable, granular
- **Envelopes (ADSR)**: Why sounds have shape over time
- **Filters in depth**: Low-pass, high-pass, bandpass, resonance, filter sweeps

### Music & Perception
- **Consonance & dissonance**: Why certain intervals sound "good" (harmonic ratios, critical bandwidth)
- **Timbre**: Why a piano and violin playing the same note sound different (harmonic envelope)
- **Psychoacoustic masking**: How loud sounds hide quiet ones (used in compression)

### Practical/Engineering
- **Latency & real-time audio**: Buffers, buffer underruns, scheduling, WebAudio timing
- **Dynamic range processing**: Compression, limiting, noise gates, side-chaining
- **Microphones & speakers**: How transducers work, frequency response curves, polar patterns

### Advanced Echo Cancellation (extends StopCopyingMe)
- **NLMS and variants**: Normalized LMS, affine projection, RLS
- **Double-talk detection**: Geigel, correlation-based, neural approaches
- **Non-linear processing**: Residual echo suppression, comfort noise
- **Beamforming**: Using multiple mics for spatial filtering

### Speech Processing
- **Formants and phonemes**: How vowels and consonants are formed
- **Pitch detection**: Autocorrelation, YIN, neural pitch trackers
- **Voice activity detection**: Energy-based, statistical, ML-based VAD
- **Noise suppression**: Spectral subtraction, Wiener filtering, neural denoisers
